Fix: only register the rewrite when mocks are off.

```ts
const useMocks = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_MOCKS === "1";

const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  ...
  async rewrites() {
    if (useMocks) return [];
    return [...];
  },
};
```

Note: importing `@/lib/mock/config` in next.config would work? Path aliases in next.config are resolved by Next's config loader (it uses jiti + tsconfig paths?). Not guaranteed. Safer to read `process.env` directly.

Also, this is an important find for the eval: in production the app talks to a deployed Render backend, not `/api/v1` locally. That means my earlier assumption ("production already uses same-origin") was wrong — production uses a rewrite. Doesn't matter with mocks on.

But also: this means the "no backend" story is different — the app normally proxies to Render. If the sandbox has egress, the app might work against Render! But no auth cookies → 401 → /login. Anyway, mock mode is the right call.

